WEBVTT

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.100
Hey, all Peter Zeihan here, coming from Colorado,

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.860
and today we're going to talk about a new sort

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.740
of targeting system that has been used in multiple

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.580
theaters or new targeting criteria,

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.040
probably the better way to phrase that.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.360
Over the weekend, in the late part of last week,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.080
we had the Houthis of Yemen starting to attack

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.560
Saudi Arabia's civilian airline system,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.200
specifically the Riyadh International Airport,

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.160
where at a minimum, 12 people were killed,

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.040
probably closer to 30,

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.640
and several hundred people were injured.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.680
Looks like a plane was hit,

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.360
one of the terminals with passengers was hit.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.960
And then in Russia,

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.680
the Ukrainians have started targeting data centers.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:37.160
Data centers are very easy to disrupt.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.120
They're very large targets.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.160
They're hard to miss,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.880
and they require absolutely massive amounts

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.040
of climate control or the chips melt down.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.160
So you put a hole in the roof,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.640
that kind of ruins the entire experience for everyone.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.000
In addition, the Russians cannot make any, any,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.640
any of the semiconductors that go into

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.160
even a circa 1999 data center.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.040
So this is 100% imported hardware that they can't

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.360
replace without spending a great deal of money.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.720
According to the Houthis,

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.440
anything that's in Saudi Arabia is a viable target because

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.000
they're in a general war with anyone who's on the other

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.760
side of the Palestinians or the Iranians.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.120
And they, over the last decade,

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.040
have really been not particularly picky about

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.480
what they attack in the first place.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.640
Ukraine is a lot more discerning.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.440
From their point of view,

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.200
data centers are part of the infrastructure

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.960
that allows Russia to be a modern state.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.560
And the data centers handle military

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.320
logistics and weapon designs,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.040
which are true.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.440
So they see it as a viable military

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.120
target in its own right,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.480
in addition to the fact that it's an important

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.840
civilian piece of infrastructure.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.640
The bottom line for both of these is that normally,

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.680
when you've got drones going against military targets,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.240
there's a degree of electronic warfare

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.720
in play that scrambles the signal.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.560
So if you've got a long-range drone coming in,

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:46.600
you can scramble their signal,

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.400
then the pilot loses control of the drone and either Peter

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:54.760
Pans or crashes or hovers and does basically no damage.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.880
Or you can kinetically intercept it with, say,

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.280
bullets or missiles or whatever it happens to be.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.720
That is not in play with these two target sets.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:04.760
Until now,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.600
the Saudis and the Russians have not put up electronic

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.800
warfare around these sort of assets.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:10.360
For one,

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:14.040
if you put electric warfare around your entire economy,

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.120
you won't have an economy anymore.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.640
It's simply too big to protect.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.480
And specifically for the airport,

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.000
if you have EW that's meaningful,

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.160
you're going to have a hard time landing planes.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.240
The bottom line is here is that

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.520
these weren't fancy drones.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:27.720
Over the last eight months,

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.760
I've done quite a few videos talking about how the advances

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.880
in drone warfare allowed them to bypass EW.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.280
That didn't apply here.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.960
These are relatively unguarded, mostly civilian targets,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.200
which means that what the Houthis and the Ukrainians

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.240
have done is eminently replicable across the entirety

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.960
of Saudi Arabia and the vast majority of Russia.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.080
Both of their systems now have more than enough range.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.560
So the Iranians are providing the Houthis

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.600
with the weapons to do this.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.360
They can hit anywhere in Saudi Arabia.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.120
The Ukrainians are, for the most part,

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.560
producing their own drones.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.480
They have already demonstrated that most of them

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.240
have a range of at least 300 kilometers,

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.760
some upwards of 1600 kilometers.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.200
So everything that's basically within 100 kilometers

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.680
of Moscow and significantly more is all within range,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.160
which means it is time for us to start noodling fast,

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:24.280
hopefully, about what a post-drone economy can even be.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.360
Because if everything within 600 miles of

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.000
an enemy is civilian infrastructure that

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.480
you either have to protect or write off,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.120
then the entire industrial age needs

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.880
to find a new way to operate.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.160
We are not ready for this.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.720
No one is ready for this.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.440
Perhaps the biggest problem that I see here is that the

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.040
drones that were used were not sophisticated at all.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.800
They don't have that advanced technology

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.880
that's being developed this year in it.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.600
These are just plain Jane weapons

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.440
platforms that are very,

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.480
very cheap.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:00.600
Nothing,

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.000
nothing in the input stream for them

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.600
is under any degree of sanctions.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.960
And if you wanted to sanction it,

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.400
you'd have to sanction basically

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.920
every single phone maker,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.240
computer maker, and most electronics makers.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.720
You're talking about chips that are not just legacy,

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.960
but all the hardware in them could have been assembled

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.520
with parts from Radio Shack 15 years ago.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.440
Was RadioShack still around 15 years ago?

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:23.720
You get the point.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.520
That's before you consider the more

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.040
advanced stuff that is coming up,

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.200
like the memory drones out of Ukraine

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.800
that can even get through jamming now.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.240
So we're now in a situation where all of

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.040
the crude out of Saudi Arabia is being threatened

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.480
not just by advanced drones,

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:40.360
but by basic ones.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.160
And the entire supporting economic structure has now,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.400
you know, basically the genie's out of the bottle,

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.360
the seal's been cracked.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.880
In the case of Russia,

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.120
it's not just about the shadow fleet and the oil market,

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.160
it's about the wheat market,

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.280
it's about the sunflower market,

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.480
it's about the iron ore market,

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.760
it's about the aluminum market,

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.040
it's about the timber market.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:01.240
All of these are now easily targeted systems with where we

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.120
are with drone manufacturing on just a regional basis.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.780
It doesn't take a huge amount of imagination to come up

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.500
with a military conflict in somebody else's backyard where

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.060
drones become part of the problem and all of a sudden

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.220
the entire industrial infrastructure is in play.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.300
I'm looking at you, Northeast Asia.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.220
Anyway, that's it from now.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.740
See you guys next time.

